content.text:
Leave that comment alone — it’s emitted by `protoc-gen-go`, not something we wrote by hand.

When Buf runs the remote Go plugin it still speaks the **protoc plugin protocol**. The generator always stamps:

```text
// Code generated by protoc-gen-go. DO NOT EDIT.
// versions:
// 	protoc-gen-go v1.36.12
// 	protoc        (unknown)
```

`(unknown)` just means the remote plugin host didn’t report a local `protoc` binary version. It does **not** mean the repo still depends on a developer-installed `protoc`.

You shouldn’t strip or edit those lines: AGENTS.md says never hand-edit plugin output, and there’s no stable `protoc-gen-go` flag to omit that header.

So: workflow is Buf-only; the header is harmless generator metadata.

